From 27e5bd2c7af6f4ad78415d3ffaa20eb23913e2ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ohos-kernel-port contributors <232252@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:08:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] include: add xpm_types.h, taken from the OpenHarmony 5.10
 tree

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Baseline: gitcode.com/openharmony/kernel_linux_6.6
Branch:   OpenHarmony-7.0-Release
Commit:   f4b61510491aa20f7f57fbbc5efc754083c92212

    include/linux/mm_types.h:22:10: fatal error: linux/xpm_types.h:
        No such file or directory

include/linux/xpm_types.h is not tracked in the 6.6 tree, and neither
struct xpm_region nor struct cs_info is defined anywhere in it.  Three files
include the header: mm_types.h, lite_hck_code_sign.h and fsverity_private.h.
mm_types.h includes it unconditionally, so disabling CONFIG_SECURITY_XPM does
not help.

The file is not invented here.  kernel_linux_5.10 in the same OpenHarmony
release carries it, and this is that file, with the SPDX tag narrowed from
GPL-2.0-or-later to GPL-2.0-only to match the 6.6 tree and the upstream
copyright left intact.

Using the real definition matters.  struct xpm_region is embedded by value in
mm_struct, so a guessed layout would have produced a kernel that compiled and
was quietly wrong.  The real one is two unsigned longs, addr_start and
addr_end, and the 5.10 and 6.6 definitions are identical.

Licence note: the file arrives as GPL-2.0-or-later in 5.10.  The 6.6 tree is
GPL-2.0-only, and GPL-2.0 section 4 forbids relicensing, so the tag is
narrowed and the original copyright retained.

Upstream: no equivalent; Linux v6.6 has no xpm_types.h.
Licence: GPL-2.0-only, same as the tree.
---
 include/linux/xpm_types.h | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/linux/xpm_types.h

diff --git a/include/linux/xpm_types.h b/include/linux/xpm_types.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a9e8afe
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/linux/xpm_types.h
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only-only */
+/*
+ * Copyright (c) 2023 Huawei Device Co., Ltd.
+ */
+
+#ifndef _XPM_TYPES_H
+#define _XPM_TYPES_H
+
+#include <linux/types.h>
+
+struct xpm_region {
+	unsigned long addr_start; /* start adress of xpm region */
+	unsigned long addr_end;   /* end address of xpm region */
+};
+
+struct cs_info {
+	uint32_t id_type;
+	uint32_t ownerid;
+};
+
+#endif /* _XPM_TYPES_H */
\ No newline at end of file
